@startuml training-ngram-pipeline
' N-gram training, both paths. The library path (TrainerBuilder::train) is a
' three-phase in-memory pipeline: parallel counting over prefetched batches, a
' second pass collecting continuation counts, and discount estimation from the
' count-of-counts. The CLI adds a second, checkpointed path selected by
' --checkpoint: a WAL-backed on-disk accumulator that survives interruption and
' is converted into an inference-format model only at the end. The two paths
' differ in whether --min-count is applied at all; that divergence is called out
' explicitly because it is a live behavioural trap.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/training-ngram-pipeline.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/training/ngram.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #263238
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title N-gram training — library path (blue) vs. checkpointed CLI path (teal)

rectangle "**CorpusReader**\nPlaintext · Wikipedia · Gutenberg" as reader #455A64
rectangle "**PrefetchingReader**\nbatch_size · ram_fraction = 0.10\nI/O decoupled from CPU" as prefetch #546E7A

rectangle "**Phase 1 — count**\nrayon par_iter over batches;\nfor n ∈ 1..=order insert every\nn-gram into the atomic trie" as count #1565C0
rectangle "**Phase 2 — continuation counts**\nN₁₊(•,w) distinct left contexts\nN₁₊(h,•) distinct right words" as cont #1565C0
rectangle "**Phase 3 — discounts**\ncount-of-counts (n₁…n₄) ⟹\nY, D₁, D₂, D₃₊ (Chen & Goodman);\nfixed fallbacks when too sparse" as disc #1565C0
rectangle "**NgramModel**\ntrie ⊕ smoothing ⊕ |V| ⊕ N" as model #1565C0

rectangle "**NgramAccumulator**\nWAL-backed on-disk counts" as accum #00838F
rectangle "**Checkpoint**\nevery ""--checkpoint-interval""\nsentences (default 1 000 000)" as ckpt #00838F
rectangle "**Finalize**\nkeep count ≥ ""--min-count"",\nload into DynamicDawgChar,\nattach Kneser-Ney smoothing" as final #00838F

rectangle "**model.bin**\nsave_portable" as out #455A64

reader --> prefetch
prefetch --> count : library path\n(no ""--checkpoint"")
count --> cont
cont --> disc
disc --> model
model --> out

reader --> accum : CLI path\n(""--checkpoint <DIR>"")
accum --> ckpt : periodic
ckpt --> accum : ""--resume""
accum --> final : end of corpus
final --> out

note bottom of count
  ""--min-count"" is **inert on this path**.
  ""TrainerBuilder::min_word_freq"" is stored on
  ""TrainingConfig"" but never read while counting,
  so the in-memory model retains every n-gram.
end note

note bottom of final
  ""--min-count"" **applies here**. Only n-grams whose
  accumulated count reaches the threshold are
  exported into the final trie.
end note

@enduml
